{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And he called Havva.</b> The vav and the yod interchange, as in הנה יד ד׳ הויה (Exodus 9:3), and אתה הוה להם למלך (Nehemiah 6:14[?]). And it is not spelled with a yod, for what difference is there between her name and the name of the living creatures?" "<b>Mother of all life.</b> Of the children of man."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The Nehemiah citation reads אתה היית in the standard text; Ibn Ezra appears to cite a variant reading with הוה, or the verse reference may be in error."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:04.058514551Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}